ARTICLE 3: ANTI-FRAGMENTATION POLICY (NO FORK)

To ensure the project's unity, the public distribution of modified, stripped-down, or derivative versions of Amentys
is strictly prohibited.

You are not authorized to publish a public "fork" of the project (for example, by replacing the official interface with
another, or by creating a separate distribution under a different name).ARTICLE 4: INTERNAL MODIFICATIONS AND PRIVACY BOUNDARIES
Private Use: You are permitted to modify the source code for your strictly private and internal use, provided that
such modifications are never publicly distributed.

Corporate and Enterprise Scope: For legal entities, "internal use" is strictly limited to deployments within the
same legal entity, accessible only by its own employees and direct contractors for internal operations. Distribution
or deployment to distinct legal entities, corporate affiliates, subsidiaries, external subcontractors, or third-party
clients is considered public distribution and is strictly prohibited.

Contribution to the Common Good: If you develop a modification, improvement, or feature that you wish to
make public, it MUST be submitted to the official Amentys repository (via a "Pull Request" or a patch). Any such
public submission is automatically governed by the assignment of rights detailed in Article 5.

