ARTICLE 15: NON-EXTRACTION AND INDIVISIBILITY OF CORE TECHNOLOGIES

Indivisible Monolith: The Software is licensed as a single, highly integrated, and indivisible product. Its core
technologies, subsystems, libraries, and proprietary engines—including, but not limited to, the jinshu architecture,
the kpack system, the SemanticRouter, and the tiered CAS memory management—are fundamentally tied to the
Amentys ecosystem.

Prohibition of Extraction (Anti-Poaching): You are strictly prohibited from decoupling, isolating, extracting, or
reverse-engineering these specific internal components or technologies for the purpose of using them
independently, integrating them into other operating systems, or packaging them as standalone libraries outside of
the official Amentys environment.

Protection of Specific Innovations: Any attempt to strip the Software of its core innovations to power external
projects, commercial or non-commercial, constitutes a direct violation of this License and an infringement of the
Original Author's intellectual property.

ARTICLE 16: HARDWARE VENDOR COMPLIANCE AND ZERO BLACK-BOX POLICY

Declarative Hardware Interfaces (No Binary Blobs): To ensure absolute security and user sovereignty, Amentys
does not permit the execution of closed-source, compiled binary drivers ("blobs") within its core architecture.
Hardware manufacturers and Original Equipment Manufacturers (OEMs) wishing to interface with the Software
MUST provide their hardware translation layers strictly as transparent, inert, and declarative semantic maps
(Refraction Plans), as defined by the Amentys documentation.

Prohibition of Telemetry and Data Exfiltration: Hardware interfaces, drivers, and translation maps submitted by
manufacturers must contain ZERO executable logic capable of intercepting, storing, or transmitting user data (e.g.,keystrokes, framebuffers, audio streams, memory states). Any inclusion of telemetry, spyware, or undocumented
data exfiltration mechanisms constitutes a severe breach of this License.

European Sovereignty and Strict Liability: If a hardware partner or manufacturer intentionally or negligently
introduces malicious logic or hidden surveillance capabilities into their Amentys-compatible interface, they will be
held strictly liable under European cybersecurity and data protection laws. The Original Author and the governing
legal entity (SASU) reserve the right to immediately revoke the manufacturer's certification, block their hardware
components across the Amentys ecosystem via semantic blacklisting, and seek unlimited financial damages for
breach of trust and ecosystem endangerment.
